  "issue": 1330,
  "title": "Support pandas nullable transaction values in missing-value mining",
  "body": "### Description\n\nEquivalent binary transaction tables currently behave differently depending on their missing-value representation. Floating NaNs work, while pandas nullable Boolean/Int64/Float64 columns and object columns containing `pd.NA` fail with an ambiguous-Boolean error.\n\nValidation now removes missing sentinels before checking observed values. The three missing-value entry points normalize validated extension/object columns to numeric NaNs in a separate frame. Ordinary numeric and sparse frames retain their existing paths. Nullable Boolean missing values are also rejected explicitly when missing values are disabled, including through the shared validation used by Apriori and H-Mine.\n\nThe original values, index, column labels, and dtypes remain unchanged. Invalid observed values are checked before conversion, so strings such as `\"1\"` are not silently accepted as binary numbers.\n\n### Related issues or pull requests\n\nCloses #1330.\n\nThis fixes input representation, independently of #1320 and earlier FP-growth candidate-pruning changes. Those algorithm changes are not included. Complete reachable histories of all four affected source modules were inspected across upstream PR refs and fork branches, including intermediate and reverted revisions; no equivalent nullable-value normalization was found.\n\n### Validation\n\n- Exact upstream base: `1aee767ef57b84a8191511a08955c583b65de382`.\n- **50 of 62 new regression cases fail on unchanged source**; all 62 pass after the change.\n- Coverage includes nullable Boolean/Int64/Float64 and object representations, mixed-column frames, all-missing frames, explicit observed-transaction support calculations, rule-metric equivalence, invalid values, missing-values-disabled behavior, input preservation, and ordinary dense/sparse controls.\n- Relevant frequent-pattern tests: **173 passed**. Complete repository suite: **802 passed, 3 skipped**.\n- Baseline and patch ran in the same Python 3.11.18 job with the unchanged frozen lock.\n- Complete repository isort/Black, changed-file Flake8, `git diff --check`, package build, and strict Twine checks passed. The repository-wide Flake8 report retains existing findings and is not presented as a clean lint gate.\n\n[Baseline and complete validation evidence](https://github.com/Afloat16/geoopt/actions/runs/43890956710/job/133381680363).\n\n### Pull Request Checklist\n\n- [x] Added a changelog entry.\n- [x] Added regression tests in the corresponding test directory.\n- [x] Documented supported missing-value representations.\n- [x] Ran focused and full repository tests.\n- [x] Checked formatting and style with the scope described above.\n",
  "status": "published",
  "base": "master",
